--TEST--
Core\Cli::secret originates a secret string that no sink will write — ADR 0086 § 4, ADR 0033 § 1
--FILE--
<?nvs
// § 4: `secret` originates a `secret tainted string`, so a password typed at a
// prompt structurally cannot be echoed, logged, dumped, put in a `Throwable`
// message or serialized. The refusal is the checker's, so it needs no terminal
// and the prompt never runs at all.
echo Core\Cli::secret("Password:");
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0790]: a `secret`-qualified value cannot be written by `echo`; output is read by a person or captured into a log, so the value would be disclosed rather than used
  --> case.nvs:6:6
